{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>באשר הוא שם</b> — according to the deeds that he does now he is judged, and not according to deeds that he is destined to do, for the ministering angels were prosecuting, etc. — this is the language of Rabbenu Shelomo, from the words of our Sages. But the correct interpretation in my eyes according to the plain sense is that when it says, \"For Elohim has heard the voice of the lad באשר הוא שם\" — in the place where he is — it informs her that she would not need to go from there to a spring or well, for in that very place he would slake his thirst immediately. And He said to her, \"Arise, lift up the lad,\" after he had drunk, \"for a great nation I will make him.\" Similarly, \"באשר כרע שם נפל שדוד\" (Judges 5:27), \"ובאשר חללים שם הוא\" (Job 39:30) — it alludes to the place:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {0 "Rabbenu Shelomo refers to Rashi (Solomon Yitzhaki). The closing phrase 'ירמוז למקום' — 'it alludes to the place' — is rendered literally; the antecedent of 'it' is ambiguous and may refer back to the verse under discussion."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:21:25.811414039Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}